<<<
spadeful. Pl. -ls; see -FUL.
===
**spadeful.** Pl. *-ls*; see ^^-FUL^^.
>>>

<<<
spare makes sparable; see MUTE E.
===
**spare** makes *sparable*; see ^^MUTE E^^.
>>>

<<<
spats. For spatterdashes; see CURTAILED WORDS.
===
**spats.** For *spatterdashes*; see ^^CURTAILED WORDS^^.
>>>

<<<
spavined, not -nned; see -N-, -NN-.
===
**spavined,** not *-nned*; see ^^-N-, -NN-^^.
>>>

<<<
spec,=speculation. CURTAILED WDS.
===
**spec,**=*speculation.* ^^CURTAILED WDS^^.
>>>

<<<
special. 1. Special) (especial. 2. S. pleading.
===
**special.** 1. *Special*) (*especial.* **2.** *S. pleading.*
>>>

<<<
1. For specially) as distinguished from espectal(ly), see ESPECIAL. The two following quotations show the adverbs used each where the other would have been better:—Ample supplies of food & clothing for the prisoners are now available there, having been shipped from America especially for this purpose./The neighbourhood ts not specially well provided
===
**1.** For *special(ly)* as distinguished from *especial(ly)*, see ^^ESPECIAL^^. The two following quotations show the adverbs used each where the other would have been better:—*Ample supplies of food & clothing for the prisoners are now available there, having been shipped from America especially for this purpose./The neighbourhood is not specially well provided*
>>>

<<<
+ with places where soldicrs can get amusement & refreshments.
===
+ *with places where soldiers can get amusement & refreshments.*
>>>

<<<
2. S. pleading is a POPULARIZED TECHNICALITY. When we say that a person’s argument is s. p., we mean that he has tried to convince us
===
**2.** *S. pleading* is a ^^POPULARIZED TECHNICALITY^^. When we say that a person's argument is s. p., we mean that he has tried to convince us
>>>

<<<
& the word special adds nothing to the meaning; why then call it special? Pleadings, in law, are a
===
& the word *special* adds nothing to the meaning; why then call it special? Pleadings, in law, are a
>>>

<<<
speciality, -alty. The two words, like many pairs in -1c(AL), while they seem to cry out for DIFFER- ENTIATION, have made little progress in that direction.
===
**speciality,** *-alty.* The two words, like many pairs in ^^-IC(AL)^^, while they seem to cry out for ^^DIFFERENTIATION^^, have made little progress in that direction.
>>>
